        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Racing Extinction, Incident at Oglala, Thunderheart, The Cove\n- People: Louie Psihoyos, Michael Apted, Robert Redford\n- Places: Lamakera, Indonesia\n- Topics: Documentaries, Anthropogenic mass extinction, Native American activism, FBI agent murders\n\nFacts:\n- In 1992, Michael Apted directed the documentary Incident at Oglala.\n- In 1992, Incident at Oglala was narrated by Robert Redford.\n- In 1992, Michael Apted had previously directed Incident at Oglala, a documentary about a Native American activist episode involving the murder of FBI agents, as referenced from Thunderheart.\n- In 2009, Louie Psihoyos directed the documentary The Cove.\n- In 2015, Racing Extinction was released as a documentary about the ongoing anthropogenic mass extinction of species and efforts by scientists, activists, and journalists to document it.\n- In 2015, Racing Extinction was directed by Oscar-winning director Louie Psihoyos.\n- In 2015, Lamakera, Indonesia, was featured in the documentary film Racing Extinction.",
